                    "line": 102,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "The lambda body here is ~19 lines; bmcweb COMMON_ERRORS.md \u00a714\nasks for <10 lines or extract to a named callback + std::bind_front:\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/master/docs/COMMON_ERRORS.md#14-very-long-lambda-callbacks\n\nSuggest splitting into `afterGetChassisProcessorLinks(asyncResp, ec, procs)`\nand binding via `std::bind_front`, matching the `afterGetXxx` pattern\nused elsewhere in bmcweb (e.g. `afterGetProcessorLocationCode`)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/chassis_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 102,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jacky Huang",
                        "email": "jackyhuang@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "jacky-c-huang"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Replaced with handleCollectionMembers."
                },
                {
